Z||000000||Haze_Performance||12-06-2000||06:26 PM|||| <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=513900316" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=513900316</A> <P>This person boosts up the bids on her LeBra.... Ive dealt with her a few times. At the last min a newly registered bidder will outbid you by a high amount.. Her real name is Ann McCreery. <P>After the auction has ended she will send you a email saying that she feels bad you lost out and she has one more left. You can buy it at your last high bid price. <P>My 2 1/2 cents: The price is good for a rare tan bra & it is new. I just dont like the dishonest bidding.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif">    <BR><B>"AHHHHH!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD!!"</B>||||reg||8
Z||000001||sqoach||12-06-2000||06:54 PM||||my mom was just telling me about people like that when i was posting my scoops. she's been over bidded on by the same person many times. she found out that it was the person selling the item, just under a different name. they bid just so you'll bid higher. and of course if they won their own item, it wouldn't matter because they already have it. some people.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>i noticed she put the shipping charges for her item. do i need to do this with mine?<BR>------------------<BR>sQoaCh<BR>fiero7@hotmail.com<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig_2.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by sqoach (edited 12-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||12-06-2000||07:43 PM||||This is called shill bidding and is obviously not allowed.  If you have concerns or proof this is going on let eBay know.  This happened to me  a year or so ago and eBay suspended the auction and kicked the seller off of eBay.<P>The problem is it is hard to prove and the seller can just open a new account under a different name.<P>At any rate, thanks for the heads up on this one.||||reg||1
